# Checked in deliberately -- none of this is secret, and it's the safety net that
# keeps a release build correct even when it's produced outside EAS (e.g. running
# `gradlew assembleRelease` directly against a locally-generated android/ project,
# which never reads eas.json). See apps/client/.env.production for the incident this
# pattern exists to prevent (a locally built release APK silently baked in
# .env.local's http://localhost:3000 because that file loads for every build type).
